# AFClaude manager container crontab for AFCLAUDE_SCHEDULER=legacy (phase 3a rollback, docs/phase3a_plan.md §4):
# docker/crontab as it was before the resident runner, frozen at step S2. With it supercronic runs every
# job, as do the watcher and the inbox API; no runner.py. Do not edit it with the cut-over steps;
# it goes away with the legacy mode (S9).
#
# AFClaude manager container crontab (supercronic, container clock = UTC like the host).
# The only AFClaude schedule (the host crontab has no AFClaude lines since 01.10.); every
# Claude-side action goes through the SSH bridge (host.py). Keep the "# AFClaude ..." tags:
# export_quickview.py lists them.
*/15 * * * * flock -n $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/.sampler.lock python3 $AFCLAUDE_DIR/usage_sampler.py >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/sampler.log 2>&1 # AFClaude usage sampler
# WINDOW-START: every 30 min (the window starts are on the 30-min grid of window_days, D-030);
# keepalive.py --window-start exits at once unless a session-window start of the configured
# windows is due in this slot (schedule.due_session_start: start + k x session_hours in window_tz,
# per weekday, also on the DST nights; D-148/D-202/D-203), and each start acts once (its dedup key,
# schedule.start_key).
*/30 * * * * cd $AFCLAUDE_DIR && python3 keepalive.py --session $AFCLAUDE_MANAGER_SESSION --window-start --arm --take-over-idle >> $KEEPALIVE_STATE_DIR/keepalive.log 2>&1 # AFClaude window-start
7,22,37,52 * * * * [ -e $AFCLAUDE_DIR/PAUSED ] || $AFCLAUDE_DIR/docker/start_watcher.sh >/dev/null 2>>$KEEPALIVE_STATE_DIR/watchdog.log # AFClaude watcher watchdog (no-op if running)
0 * * * * cd $AFCLAUDE_DIR && python3 usage_review.py >> $KEEPALIVE_STATE_DIR/keepalive.log 2>&1 # AFClaude usage-model review (runs when its state's next_run_at, in the DB, has passed)
*/3 * * * * flock -n $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/.quickview.lock python3 $AFCLAUDE_DIR/export_quickview.py >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/quickview_export.log 2>&1 # AFClaude quickview export
*/10 * * * * cd $AFCLAUDE_DIR && python3 dispatcher.py --arm --once >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/dispatcher.log 2>&1 # AFClaude dispatcher (10-min pass: cleanup, health checks, approved stalled sessions at their reset at any time; starts no runs, D-205/D-206)
* * * * * python3 $AFCLAUDE_DIR/docker/at_shim.py --run-due >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/at_shim.log 2>&1 # AFClaude at-shim (the jobs in the DB: the sampler's pre/post weekly-reset samples, one-off reviews)
# DOCS IMPORT: every 10 min (design §7.7): hand edits of PROGRESS.md / GOALS.md / EXCEPTIONS.md
# (and a legacy ALERTS.md / data/reviews/*.md) into the project docs in the DB (doc.sync, actor
# runner:import; merged with the runners' notes, files never written; a conflict alerts once).
# Prints a line only when something was imported.
*/10 * * * * flock -n $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/.docs_import.lock python3 $AFCLAUDE_DIR/project_docs.py import --cron >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/docs_import.log 2>&1 # AFClaude docs import
# INBOX API WATCHDOG: inbox_api.py serve (the message box to the task-manager, D-241) is started by the
# entrypoint; this starts it again if it died, and alerts that it was not running.
*/5 * * * * cd $AFCLAUDE_DIR && python3 inbox_api.py ensure >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/inbox_api.log 2>&1 # AFClaude inbox API watchdog (no-op if running)
# RETENTION: once a day, off-peak; deletes app_log rows past log_retention_days /
# log_retention_overrides (actions.SETTINGS), batched and audited (actor runner:retention,
# store.prune_app_log; D-161/D-130 -- app_log lines only, never telemetry/usage data).
17 3 * * * flock -n $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/.prune_logs.lock python3 $AFCLAUDE_DIR/store.py prune-logs >> $AFCLAUDE_DIR/data/prune_logs.log 2>&1 # AFClaude log retention
